## TLDR

**A deterministic sub-quantum field theory obeying O1 (definite substrate) and O2 (field monism) CAN reproduce CHSH above 2 up to exactly 2√2 — by relaxing measurement independence (MI), and only that — but the required source–setting correlation is postulated, not derivable from the fabric dynamics, and the relaxation mechanism itself contains no Tsirelson ceiling.** All seven brief deliverables are in `v87/FABLE_WORK.md` with runnable worksheets in `v87/work/fable/` (SymPy + Maxima + Monte Carlo, all passing).

**The construction (F2).** λ ∈ S² with local deterministic responses A = sgn(a·λ), B = −sgn(b·λ), and a measurement-dependent source density ρ_p(λ|b) ∝ |λ·b|^p. I derived the closed form E_p(θ) = −1 + ((p+1)/π)·B((p+2)/2,½)·∫₀^θ sin^p φ dφ by machine-checked steps (Maxima proves the key identity exactly). p=0 is the local sawtooth (S ≤ 2); **p=1 gives E = −cosθ, the exact quantum singlet, hence S = 2√2**; p→∞ runs to the PR box S = 4. Monte Carlo with explicit PRNG confirms all three regimes at 0.8σ with N = 2×10⁷.

**The price, exact (F3).** Two tight laws: S ≤ 2 + 2D in summed total variation (LP-verified tight, D = √2−1 at Tsirelson), and the minimal mutual information curve **I_min(S) = D_KL((1+S/4)/2 ‖ 3/4)** — 0.046274 bits/run at 2√2, log₂(4/3) ≈ 0.415 bits at the PR box.

