**Honest negatives (the crux).** S_max(p) passes smoothly through 2√2 with nothing structural at p=1 — the Tsirelson bound is imported by matching QM, not derived from the relaxation. Doors B and C are closed for the actual kernel: the measured 1–5% preferred frame is dispersion, not a nonlocal channel, and the leapfrog integrator has no two-time boundary structure. The measured mixing character of the fabric dynamics points *against* deriving the needed conspiracy. Sharpest falsifiable consequence: the kernel as-is predicts |S| ≤ 2 for any in-fabric Bell test, and any Door-A completion predicts S degrades along the inverted price curve (I = 0.01 bits → S ≤ 2.40) when setting entropy is genuinely fresh.
